            "title_en": "Memo: Trial Run of Optical Parcel Sorting System in Zone B",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "block_id": "ag-blk-p6-000002-1",
                "type": "text",
                "text_en": "To: All Distribution Center Supervisors\nFrom: Marcus Vance, Director of Warehouse Operations\n\nStarting next Monday, Zone B will begin a two-week operational trial of our new optical parcel sorting conveyor. The equipment is designed to process up to 3,500 packages per hour, [[blank:ag-i-p6-000002-1]] reducing manual scanning bottlenecks during peak evening shifts. During the initial phase, only standard rectangular cartons weighing under twenty kilograms will be routed through the automated lane. [[blank:ag-i-p6-000002-2]] Floor supervisors must ensure that all shift leads complete the safety checklist [[blank:ag-i-p6-000002-3]] activating the conveyor belts each morning. Any barcode recognition errors should be logged in the shared maintenance spreadsheet so our engineers can calibrate [[blank:ag-i-p6-000002-4]] before full deployment in December."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "speakers": [],
        "audio_script": []
      },
